  <article class="post">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="post-head">
        <span class="mono label meta">Studio · 17 August 2026 · 5 min read</span>
        <h1>A podcast studio in Setúbal, ready when you are.</h1>
        <p class="dek">A proper soundproofed room to record a podcast or video, with the acoustics, the light and the gear already sorted. Book it by the hour, 35 minutes from Lisboa.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="post-hero"><img src={hero} alt="The soundproofed podcast and content studio at 22cowork in Setúbal" /></div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>Recording a podcast at home almost works. Then the neighbour drills, a car goes by, the room echoes, and an hour of good conversation is unusable. What you actually need is a treated room that does one job well, and you don't want to build one yourself. That's exactly what our <strong>podcast studio in Setúbal</strong> is for.</p>

        <p>It sits inside 22cowork, 35 minutes south of Lisboa, and you can book it by the hour without being a member.</p>

        <h2>Why record here instead of at home</h2>
        <p>The difference you hear first is the silence. The room is <strong>soundproofed and acoustically treated</strong>, so there's no echo, no street, no fridge hum bleeding into your audio. The difference you see is the light: controlled studio lighting instead of whatever your window is doing that day. And the difference you feel is that everything is already set up, so you walk in, sit down and record, rather than spending the first hour fighting your setup.</p>

        <blockquote>A good studio isn't about more gear. It's a room that removes every reason a recording goes wrong.</blockquote>

        <h2>What's in the room</h2>
        <p>A <strong>soundproofed, acoustically panelled space</strong> for clean audio. Professional lighting for video and thumbnails that look the part. Microphones and a recording setup ready to go. Space for a two to four person conversation around the table, so it works for interviews as well as solo episodes. If you bring your own kit, there's room and power for it too.</p>

        <h2>Who it's for</h2>
        <p>Podcasters who want their audio to sound professional from episode one. YouTubers and short-form creators who need clean video and light. Course and content creators recording lessons or talking-head pieces. And founders recording an occasional interview or announcement who don't want to rent a full production studio for an afternoon. If you record anything, the room pays for itself in the time and re-takes it saves.</p>

        <h2>Setúbal, not a studio across the city</h2>
        <p>You get a real studio without the Lisboa commute or the Lisboa price. Park underground, walk in, record, leave. For creators already on the peninsula it's minutes from home, and for anyone coming from the capital it's a short drive against the traffic. It's part of the same reason <a href="/blog/setubal-tech-hub">people are building here</a> at all: the serious infrastructure moved south.</p>

        <h2>How booking works</h2>
        <p>The studio is available <strong>by the hour</strong>, and members on the right plan get included studio time as part of their contract. You book the slot, the room is yours, and everything is ready when you arrive. If you're not sure it fits what you record, the simplest thing is to come see it.</p>
        <hr />
        <p class="mono">Work here too? See <a href="/#spaces">the desks and offices</a>, or read our guide to <a href="/blog/working-remotely-from-setubal">working remotely from Setúbal</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="post-cta">
        <h3>Book the studio.</h3>
        <p>A soundproofed room with light and mics, ready to record, in Setúbal. Tell us your slot and we'll confirm within a day.</p>
        <a href="/#reserve" class="btn btn-gold">Book the studio →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
